Z||000005||Tonker||09-10-2001||12:49 AM||||I have a '92 Geo Metro, my student car. It's great on gas and with some winter tires should stick to the roads quite happily. They're also dirt cheap. Oh and mine has cost me almost nothing since I've owned - very reliable little car.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sootah||09-10-2001||01:29 AM||||How are Fieros in the winter? Bout to get one for relatively cheap, was planning on making it look pretty and selling it to get a better one (GT or at least a manual) but I may keep it around if they work well in the winter.<P>------------------<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I><BR>AIM: KSSouter||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||09-10-2001||01:40 AM||||Fiero's are actually very good in the winter.  Especially the 4 bangers.  Lot's of weight over the rear wheels.  I made it home through a blizzard with 12+ inches of snow on the ground in my 84 SC.  That's one of the struggles I'm facing right now.. my 84 has been sitting for about 2 years, need's new brakes.  Have to decide if I want to fix it up and use it as a winter car or get something else and part out the 84..||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||09-10-2001||09:05 AM||||I have the ULTIMATE winter beater for you snow dwellin folks. I still have my 88 Mazda 323 GTX for sale. AWD, turbo 16v 153hp, less then 100k. I'm tellin ya, this baby is a hell of a deal. Reduced to $800!||||reg||1
