Z||000014||Fformula88||09-10-2001||04:42 PM||||&lt;~~~ Winter?  Snowy driving?? I wouldn't know anything about that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Because we see 150-200 inches a winter, I am very pro-AWD/4WD vehicles for winter cars.  I think Geo/Chevy Trackers are good winter beaters... Fairly new ones with next to no milage are dirt cheap!  It'll last you a while, they hold up well, and their a lot of fun in their own way.  Look for a convertable with the optional hardtop!  Can br fun in the summer too (while upgrading the Fiero of course).<P>As for cars, I drive a 97 Probe in the winter (really year round.  I don't take my Fiero downtown to work!).  With a good set of tires its not bad.  The back end is light and does get a little loose in snow.  Celica may exhibit the same tendancy.  <P>My father has driven a Fiero year round since 1990.  Never got it stuck in snow, but it will start to lift off the wheels when the snow gets deep.  You just have to know its limits and not try to go thru two feet of white stuff.  Otherwise it handled fine.  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jaygee79||09-10-2001||10:24 PM||||I use my Fiero in the winter.  It's actually pretty good.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ranger Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Uaana||09-11-2001||01:47 AM||||Ok found another one to add to the list.<BR>Mazda MX6<BR>Anyone have thoughts or opinions on these?<BR>Looks like the baby subaru is out.. <BR>Read some bad things on consumer reports about them.<BR>The Celica is still a maybe. little too rusty for my taste though.||||reg||1
Z||000017||k2m4||09-11-2001||02:11 PM||||get your self a nice fiero 4 banger for a couple hundred bucks ...best winter car i ever drove is my fiero .!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000018||Fformula88||09-11-2001||02:21 PM||||See my comments on the Probe... they are the SAME car underneath the sheet metal.  Again, not bad.  I have owned two a 91 and a 97 Probe.  Both extremely reliable and rugged.  The 91 was great in snow, the 97 a little loose in the back.  The 97 als has wider tires (its equipped with a handling package).  Might be the difference.  Just watch out for 94-97 4 cyl auto's.  Those trannies aren't the most reliable.||||reg||1
